`,s.jsxs(e.p,{children:["Backward accumulates the gradients straight into ",s.jsx(e.code,{children:"grad_buffer"}),", as long as the trainer zeroes them in place instead of setting them to ",s.jsx(e.code,{children:"None"}),". The all-gather writes straight into the parameters. Megatron-LM's distributed optimizer and DeepSpeed's ZeRO both keep the parameters in contiguous buffers like this. Megatron-LM keeps the gradients in one as well. FSDP1's ",s.jsx(e.code,{children:"FlatParameter"})," is the same idea. DDP's counterpart is ",s.jsx(e.code,{children:"gradient_as_bucket_view=True"}),": each ",s.jsx(e.code,{children:".grad"})," is then a view into its bucket."]}),`
